    "doc_text": "XIN_ENG_20061108.0218\n\nNEW YORK, Nov. 8 , 2006 (Xinhua)\n\nU.S. stocks open lower\n\n\n\n\nU.S. stocks opened lower on Wednesday as America's midterm election results became known.\n\nIn the opening trading, the Dow Jones Industrial Average was down 15.80, to 12,140.97. The Standard  Poor's 500 index lost 0.34 to 1,382.50, and the Nasdaq composite index fell 11.96 to 2,363.92.\n\nCrude oil prices rose slightly on Wednesday amid supply concerns in Nigeria, the largest African oil producer.\n\nWhile the Democrats won control of the House of Representatives for the first time in 12 years in Tuesday's mid-term legislative elections, the Senate race is still too close to call.",
